    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        425,
        1509,
        1387,
        1620
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "To preserve continuity in the operation of government, I have today continued the effec-\ntiveness of virtually all the Executive Orders issued by prior Mayors. This does not mean, how-\never, that I am approving the content or substance of all those orders. To the contrary, I am\nordering my Counsel to make a complete review of the entire group of Executive Orders. Those\nwhich do not reflect the policy of my Administration will be changed.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.1699,
          "min": -0.8198
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 91,
          "mean": -0.0097,
          "min": -0.8661
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 19811,
        "area_px": 108416,
        "density": 0.18273,
        "chars": 441,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 22.26
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        425,
        1620,
        1389,
        1730
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "In addition, some of the orders deal with the structure and organization of the Govern-\nment, which I intend to modify. For example, the structure of the management and budget\nfunctions must conform to my Administration's arrangements. Thus, the continuation of orders\nshould not create any expectations that the status quo will be maintained. Furthermore, obsolete\norders may be repealed and certain offices abolished.\n\nj9-13",
